  "notes": "**Renamed programs.** The names no longer clash with Aether HF, so both can be installed on the same computer:\n\n| Before (0.1.0) | Now |\n|---|---|\n| `aetherd` (engine) | `aetherdv` |\n| `aether-cli` | `aetherdv-cli` |\n| `aether-bench` | `aetherdv-bench` |\n| `aether-rfd` (ratflector server) | `aetherdv-rfd` |\n| `aecap` (capture reader) | `aetherdv-cap` |\n| `aetherd.token` | `aetherdv.token` |\n| `AETHER_TOKEN_FILE`, `AETHER_API` | `AETHERDV_TOKEN_FILE`, `AETHERDV_API` |\n\nUnchanged:\n- **Configuration files:** no edits needed.\n- **Capture files:** `.aecap` still reads as before.\n- **API address:** still `127.0.0.1:7373` by default.\n\nIf you start the engine yourself, use `aetherdv --config \u2026` and point the app at `aetherdv.token`. The app starts the bundled engine under its new name automatically.\n\nStill **tested in simulation only**: no tests with real D-RATS stations, real radios or over the air yet.",
